{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pulls/22","id":4887433179,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVLzC488AAAABI1BP2w","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pull/22","diff_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pull/22.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pull/22.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/issues/22","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pulls/22/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pulls/22/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/issues/22/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/statuses/84f49159b066faa87a135c0662f9eba5be971e10","number":22,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"A01: build pinned Asterinas and retain actual QEMU input snapshots","user":{"login":"Franksudoman","id":273670192,"node_id":"U_kgDOEE_gMA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/273670192?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman","html_url":"https://github.com/Franksudoman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR vendors the complete pinned Asterinas v0.19.0 derivative under the single `kernel/asterinas/` root, retaining upstream source, documentation, licenses and attribution. The developer build entries invoke upstream `make kernel` and `make run_kernel` with a small initramfs. The pin remains `c4b7ed575b7b32773475b194d2ad41fb6d03765b`, Rust `nightly-2026-07-21`; root README is zero bytes and this phase changes no kernel/core/OSTD source.\n\nThe latest fixes complete early `CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS` presence rejection across the four build/test/debug/integration entries, including an empty value, before consuming outputs or tools. QEMU now loads retained private copies of its actual kernel/initramfs inputs, verified before and after execution. Source-path metadata and original argv remain available. Actual main `bc294f75bfb8c03d9963f5a12ea23b9589779d96` was integrated through merge `be86dc41228078b4b941b8a2e4d745fc09453d11`; its approved owner code was imported unchanged.\n\n| Validation | Actual result and scope |\n| --- | --- |\n| New debug/integration entry guards | 56 passing host executions across isolated ordinary/optimized Python; original red assertions and old/fixed CLI probes retained. |\n| QEMU input snapshots | 52 passing host executions; original checker unchanged; replacement failure retained. |\n| TCP/GDB OSDK matrix at `071dd8edcd2a3cf9b33dbbeab713428317b9b76c` | 22/22, eleven real QEMU guests raw33, one VMX soft skip. Explicit TCP profile; no default-UNIX or coverage-percentage claim. |\n| Full Asterinas Rust-entry debug at `31170ffb2ab6d18a85051d426e5d85a83f1b2abf` | GDB PC and 32 live instruction bytes match `__ostd_main`; detach followed by complete initramfs boot, raw33. x86_64/q35/TCG, one vCPU, 512 MiB; independent fresh live-artifact checker exit0. |\n| Current-main host validation | 83 Rust passes, including one doctest, plus 98 Python passes = 181 executions. Both fmt and control strict Clippy exit0. ABI strict Clippy exits101 in three test helpers: overall validation remains partial. |\n| A02 isolated candidate | Three-helper patch passes fixed-nightly 61 tests, fmt, no_std target check and strict Clippy. Its 14 inputs match current main and fresh apply-check exits0. Pending A00/A02 adoption; owner source remains unmodified. |\n\nThe successful debug run reused the DWARF artifact actually produced at `071dd8ed...`, with zero new compiling lines. It is a cached debug retry, not a fresh-target rebuild. Earlier clean-target source builds, normal boots and OSTD/core regressions keep their original source bindings and denominators. No Linux host or ISO-installer boot is counted as kernel acceptance.\n\nThe actual QEMU-loaded successful debug ELF is 5,975,720 bytes, SHA256 `fbe81c0e2deae705d61d77ccaaf604e2bf1ca30e4541de71d263af6ecc62ec1b`. Complete serial/GDB/commands, actual boot snapshots, original failed attempts, coverage counters, checksum/member indexes and the full 111 MB symbol ELF are retained. The symbol gzip is stored losslessly as 13 ordered chunks with reconstruction verification.\n\nReview/replay:\n- [Current-main validation report](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/blob/agents/A01-asterinas-boot/support/build/evidence/2026-10-16-cloud-main-sync/REPORT.md)\n- [Cloud closure report, real debug artifacts and A05/A06 interface table](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/blob/agents/A01-asterinas-boot/support/build/evidence/2026-10-16-blocker-closure/REPORT.md)\n- [A02 candidate patch and owner handoff](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/blob/agents/A01-asterinas-boot/support/build/handoffs/a02-nightly-clippy/README.md)\n\nRemaining work includes supported KVM/VMX execution for the three earlier VMX/EPT skips; host AF_UNIX EPERM blocking two default-profile cases; cross-path/cross-host reproducibility and an immutable environment; unknown external artifact writer attribution; historical A04 two fd-limit failures/two SCM_RIGHTS timeouts; and A05/A06/A07 native G1/G2/runtime/Hepta owner integration. Infrastructure validation does not establish those features. Failed debug/OSDK attempts and all strict-Clippy diagnostics remain failures in their original evidence. Queued remote CI is not green.\n\nPublished head: `01a344c6a293fd73b158e9e6ca93bd9904b69bbf`. Integrated main: `bc294f75bfb8c03d9963f5a12ea23b9589779d96`. This PR targets main from `agents/A01-asterinas-boot`; A00 retains merge ownership.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-16T11:04:01Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T01:12:49Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"3074a5bd5f505da67a114093fd0964bcac4dfbb0","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"TrillionniumFoundation:agents/A01-asterinas-boot","ref":"agents/A01-asterinas-boot","repo":{"id":1421656803,"node_id":"R_kgDOVLzC4w","name":"trillionnium-os-desktop","full_name":"TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop","owner":{"login":"TrillionniumFoundation","id":262513357,"node_id":"O_kgDOD6WizQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262513357?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/subscriptions","